    {
      "id": "MSC-02",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-mixed-casimir-value",
      "title": "The scalar of the mixed compact Casimir on one summand",
      "statement": "For the ordered-pair convention κ(η)=‖η+ρ_c‖²−‖ρ_c‖², the position Casimir is m on opposite-sign directions. On a compact summand of weight μ=Λ+e_a−e_b, Ω=ΣP_cd D_dc acts by (κ(μ)−m−κ(Λ))/2.",
      "hypotheses": "The compact generator sum includes all ordered equal-sign pairs including equal indices. There is one noncompact tensor position. The direction action is the commutator, and the independent action on S is the differential of the compact representation.",
      "correspondence": "The text evaluates diagonal and raising/lowering Casimir contributions on a highest vector and uses trace-pairing invariance to extend the scalar to its span. The double commutator calculation counts the p+s indices in the two opposite sign blocks. This yields the same one-slot identity as the source Casimir expansion.",
      "dependencies": [
        "MSC-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "normalization-compact-casimir-scalar",
        "normalization-mixed-casimir-scalar"
      ],
